import importlib.util,json
from pathlib import Path
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('g',H.with_suffix('.py'));g=importlib.util.module_from_spec(s);s.loader.exec_module(g)
source=json.loads((H/'source.json').read_text());qs=source['record'][':knowledge-point/questions']
classification=['# Classification','Captured math basis 1356; lineage '+source['lineage']+'. Twelve practice sources: six easy, six moderate; no observed hard. Every source has one radio field (`selection`), five text options, a correct designation, difficulty and worked solution. No plots, omissions, duplicate fields or unresolved mathematical errors were found. Canonical example e-21813 is supporting context, not a practice source.','There are two broad recognition backbones (select homogeneous / select inhomogeneous), implemented as six source prose/layout masks at each level to retain every distinct operative sentence and stage sequence. Source q-331725 uses two collect-y chains and all-homogeneous classification; q-331742 has a constant y coefficient and reduces it without a grouped polynomial. Complete bank membership is tracked per source even where multiple sources share the same bank set.','| Source | Level | a x^n | RHS triples (b,c,m): by+cx^m | Complete profile | Plot |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for q in qs:
 id=q[':question/math-academy-id'];r=g.RECIPES[id];p=r['parameters'];classification.append('| '+id+' | '+r['level']+' | '+str(p['a'])+' x^'+str(p['n'])+' | '+json.dumps(p['rhs'])+' | raw_'+id+' / observed_'+id+' | none |')
classification+=['## Curriculum and missing hard scope','The activity route was reconstructed from activity/first-step and step/next: introduction (17592186088797), standard form tutorial (88798), writing standard form KP (88799), identifying linear ODEs KP (88800), homogeneous/inhomogeneous tutorial (88801), this KP (88802). The owning topic is Introduction to First-Order Linear ODEs (MA 906), preceded by Introduction to Differential Equations (MA 3215). Subsequent integrating-factor, Laplace-transform and homogeneous-substitution topics are outside scope.','Authored hard retains three given first-order linear equations and the five-option radio selection. Each equation requires moving exactly one y term and one forcing term, collecting like terms, then dividing by a nonzero constant k=2..5. Two forcing terms cancel identically and one does not. This adds the already-taught standard-form bookkeeping to the existing recognition decision without solving any equation. All hard instances have the same four rows per equation and integer coefficients of magnitude at most 5, powers 1..3. This is a design claim, not a recovered MA difficulty label. Easy and moderate labels are preserved exactly; their source distinction is the requested categorical criterion, not invented algebra difficulty.']
(H/'classification.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(classification)+'\n')
extraction=['# Four-stage template extraction','## 1. Specific source descriptions','All original number forms, prompts, banks and prose are preserved in source.json and shown in review.md. The table in classification.md records every original coefficient, exponent, equation order and zero/y/forcing role. Easy asks for homogeneous equations; moderate asks for inhomogeneous equations. All use y(x), prime notation, three bullet equations, text subset answers and a single selection radio. The coefficients are small signed integers; forcing is zero, a constant or monomial, or a y term that must be moved. There are no rational/singular coefficient functions or domain exclusions.','## 2. Shared mathematical pattern','The invariant is a first-order linear ODE. Move every y term to the left, normalize the derivative coefficient where needed, and inspect the resulting forcing function as an identity in x, rather than its value at one point. Source examples with x or x^3 on the right remain inhomogeneous even when that forcing vanishes at x=0. Each solution examines the equations in displayed order and concludes with a subset of Roman positions.','## 3. Components and complete-bank mapping','Each observed profile below lists every source choice one-to-one. Since these answers are subsets, recipes are exact categorical selection mistakes rather than numerical perturbations. A singleton may select only one inspected equation; the all-three response treats all equally; a pair includes or excludes another equation. No specific historical learner misconception is inferred beyond the exact subset selected. Identical bank membership across sources does not imply an authoring algorithm. Raw profiles are explicitly evidence-only; observed profiles use the exact same supported full bank in normal generation.']
for q in qs:
 id=q[':question/math-academy-id'];r=g.RECIPES[id]
 extraction+=['### '+id, 'Original parameters: `'+json.dumps(r['parameters'])+'`. Correct subset: **'+r['correct']+'**.','| Source option | Parameterized categorical operation | Reproduced |','|---|---|---|']
 for a in q[':question/answer-fields'][0][':answer-field/choices']:
  v=a[':answer/value'];extraction.append('| '+v+' | Select exactly the displayed Roman positions '+v+' | yes |')
 extraction+=['Prompt mask:\n```text\n'+r['problem_mask']+'\n```','Worked-solution mask (full shared prose and operative stages):\n```text\n'+r['solution_mask']+'\n```']
extraction+=['## 4. Reusable backbone and slots','Each source mask uses whole equation slots eq0..eq2, aligned originals, the expanded move-y rows, the collected-y row, and complete forcing operands. No short substring is substituted across prose or function notation. Original-mask rendering reproduces the whole decoded prompt and solution byte-for-byte. The normal path uses the same shared prose and stage masks under changed parameters. Labels/order are held by the chosen source layout; all observed layouts are eligible in default sampling.','Allowed slots: a has source sign and |a|=1..9; n remains 0 for the constant-coefficient mask and otherwise ranges 1..3. A y RHS has the observed sign, |b|=1..5, and c=m=0. A nonzero forcing has |c|=1..9, either fixed m=0 for constant-forcing masks or m=1..3 for monomials. A zero RHS stays (0,0,0). Constant-coefficient instances reject a=b to retain collection workload. The whole bank is chosen before these parameters; no option replacement or pooled-first-valid recipes are used. All explicit inputs enforce the same bounds.','Hard uses exactly three rows of (k,a,n,b,d,e,m), rendered as k y′ + a x^n y + d x^m = b y + e x^m. k=2..5, |a|,|b|,|d|,|e|=1..5, n,m=1..3; d=e for two positions and d!=e for the bank’s selected nonzero-forcing position. All x are real and division is only by the nonzero integer k, so domains are established before cancellation. Its three complete banks are the observed I/II/III single-correct banks, selected before sampling. Stage sequence: original, move-y (separate terms), collect y and forcing, divide to standard form, inspect forcing, conclude.','Meaningful categorical variety is finite. Magnitudes, variable lettering and option order do not create new semantic fingerprints. Source-layout roles, forcing type, requested criterion, constant-coefficient collection and normalization workload do. The complete policy has 15 categorical task fingerprints: six easy source role/layout demands, six moderate demands, and three hard nonzero-forcing positions. Independent coefficient/power values provide valid practice objects at the same method; they do not inflate that finite count. Do not describe the numerical parameter count as infinitely many skills.','There are no source repairs. Source q-331725 concludes “I, II and III,” while its bank spells “I, II, and III”; the exact prose is retained and the validator recognizes their identical subset meaning. Raw records preserve all source question/field/answer attribute-presence after removing EDB internal numeric IDs and normalizing schema enum/correct-reference representation to the required local review shape. UUID identity is regenerated and field-owned. source.json retains the untouched capture including internal IDs. No original omissions were present.','Validation reads concrete equations, all initial/intermediate/final operands and forcing values back from actual learner strings. Every intermediate equation must be equivalent after nonzero derivative normalization to its own prompt equation. Required expanded/collected/divided structures are checked separately from equality. Native grading selects each owned UUID and requires exactly the derived correct subset to pass. Mutation regressions corrupt a sign, remove an expanded row, stale the conclusion, or insert a control byte.']
(H/'template-extraction.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(extraction)+'\n')
(H/'plot-extraction.md').write_text('# Plot extraction / step 7\n\nPlot rating: none for all observed and authored templates. The complete captured prompt, bank and solution contain no image or mathematical graph references. No renderer, plot asset or diagram is needed.\n')
